# Crossroads go every 27 cells, so the streets make a grid of squares. A road
# laid on towards another road never runs onto it, nor ends at a crossroads:
# it stops with a cell of grass between.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> expect cannot build crossroads at s0:40 every 27 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s0:40: Crossroads go only every 27 cells
> build crossroads at s0:55
  #1 intersection at s0:55-57, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:56 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> expect cannot build road at s1:131 end of a road
  ok: can't build road at s1:131: Roads go only at the end of a road
> lay road 8
  s1 now runs cells 121..165
> expect cannot build crossroads at s1:151 every 27 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s1:151: Crossroads go only every 27 cells
> ride s1:158
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #15 intersection at s1:157-159, done
> ride #last
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s2:131 facing +
> lay road 12
  s2 now runs cells 121..177
> build crossroads at s0:28
  #28 intersection at s0:28-30, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:29 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s3:131 facing +
> lay road 4
  s3 now runs cells 121..153
# the next block would come within a cell of the road along row AB
> expect cannot build road at s3:153 another road is in the way
  ok: can't build road at s3:153: Another road is in the way
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 10..252
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 121..165, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 121..177, from crossroads #15
  s3  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 121..153, from crossroads #28
    crossroads #1: s0:56 = s1:131 (cell A56)
    crossroads #15: s1:158 = s2:131 (cell AB56)
    crossroads #28: s0:29 = s3:131 (cell A29)
